# Everything else is left to core.autocrlf, which is how this repository has always
# handled line endings. These two are exceptions because they are read inside Linux
# images, where a carriage return is part of the command rather than invisible: a
# script checked out with CRLF fails at its own shebang, and a container definition
# with CRLF can break a line continuation.
*.sh text eol=lf
Containerfile* text eol=lf
